1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:25,981
A nigga offered me six hundred million for Isla Gloria before I
finished my first breakfast as its owner. Cream suit. Briefcase.
Polished shoes he kept checking against the terrace stones. He
approached while Shawna was eating strawberries and I was enjoying the
view from directly across the table. Captain Aiden. An exceptional
acquisition. Nigga, it's breakfast. I refer to the island.

2
00:00:26,231 --> 00:00:48,331
I refer to the strawberries. He smiled carefully and opened the case.
Papers. Pen. The number displayed where I could see it. Six hundred
million. I looked. Shawna selected another strawberry. No. The man's
fingers paused on the pen. You haven't considered the offer. Nigga,
she picked the curtains. Shawna laughed.

3
00:00:48,581 --> 00:01:07,019
He looked toward the palace windows, apparently hoping the curtains
might be cheaper to negotiate with. Those can be included. They
already are, she said. They're in our house. He tried a larger number.
I took a strawberry. He explained opportunities. Shawna poured more
coffee.

4
00:01:07,269 --> 00:01:31,682
He used the phrase liquid position, and I pointed at the sea before my
wife caught my wrist and lowered it. Behave. Nigga brought that phrase
to my ocean. She shook with laughter. The man capped his pen. Uncapped
it. Nigga couldn't find a financial instrument that would make either
of us stop enjoying breakfast. Is there a figure you'd entertain?
She's sitting right there.

5
00:01:31,932 --> 00:01:54,235
Shawna threw her napkin at me. All right, that one's terrible. Nigga,
I'm off duty. The visitor closed his briefcase. She thanked him for
coming, which was considerably nicer than the farewell I had prepared.
We watched him cross the terrace, still protecting the shoes. Then she
leaned over and kissed me. You like money. Love money. Love me more?

6
00:01:54,485 --> 00:02:12,279
Nigga, money don't look at me like that. She gave me the last
strawberry and moved her chair around beside mine. I made room. The
ocean stayed exactly where she'd asked me to bring her. We stayed
three more days. Long enough for the island to become more than the
finish line.

7
00:02:12,529 --> 00:02:33,930
Long enough to learn which bakery opened first, which balcony got the
evening breeze, which road made Shawna lean against the window and
stop talking because the view had found the quiet part of her. I drove
her around the coast in the blue Ferrari. Slowly sometimes. Nigga, I
know. Nobody tell the commentators.

8
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:56,539
They would have spent twenty minutes investigating whether I had been
replaced. We stopped at the little beach beneath the eastern cliffs.
White sand. Clear water. No palace visible from it, no flags, no
trophy ceremony waiting to begin. Shawna took off her shoes and walked
straight into the sea. I followed. The water reached our knees.

9
00:02:56,789 --> 00:03:18,097
She turned toward me with her dress gathered in one hand. This is what
I asked for. I looked around. All that racing for this little patch?
She splashed me. Nigga, don't make the ocean regret choosing us. I
caught her around the waist and lifted her out of the water. She
laughed, arms around my neck, feet bright in the sun.

10
00:03:18,347 --> 00:03:39,621
For a while there was nobody to impress except the woman already
holding me like I had won. I impressed her anyway. Habit. In town, the
old race posters came down. New ones went up with all five finalists
on them, though the printer made my photograph twice as large and
claimed it was necessary for balance.

11
00:03:39,871 --> 00:04:03,541
Sabine sent me a message saying she had never seen balance work so
much like vanity. I sent her a signed poster. She asked for three
more. Adrian paid his remaining wagers without complaint and invited
me to race his new boat the following summer. Nigga, I told him, you
sure you can afford friendship? He laughed. I can't afford another
enemy like you.

12
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:26,008
Rafe came to the palace with flowers for Inez and a bottle for me. He
apologized for the things he'd said before he knew us. I told him if I
refused every nigga who had doubted me, I'd spend my whole life eating
alone. He stayed for lunch. So did Sabine. So did half the harbor once
somebody heard Rosa was singing in the garden.

13
00:04:26,258 --> 00:04:41,271
The palace learned what a table was for. Mercedes and Porsche spent
the days finishing No Second Door. They chose Alina as their local
partner, gave her a real share and asked her opinion before buying the
chairs.

14
00:04:41,521 --> 00:05:05,747
She cried at the question, which made Mercedes furious on her behalf,
then made her sit down and choose the fucking chairs before the tears
dried into indecision. Lark and Mateo opened the garage with six of
the rescued mechanics. The sign read RED SAINT WORKS. Beneath it, in
smaller letters, Mateo had added CARS RETURNED ALIVE WHEN POSSIBLE.

15
00:05:05,997 --> 00:05:25,844
Lark pointed at me when I read it. That line is for you. Nigga, my
vehicles have rich experiences. They have rich owners. There's a
difference. Mateo laughed, and she kissed him without stopping her
argument. His plant had survived in their mainland apartment. A
neighbor had watered it.

16
00:05:26,094 --> 00:05:46,235
He brought it to the island himself and placed it in the garage window
like it had also been rescued from a difficult month. Inez and Cassius
postponed choosing a wedding date until they could get through one
dinner without both fathers arguing about the cars in the procession.
Nero wanted the White Heron.

17
00:05:46,485 --> 00:06:08,878
Esteban wanted the Red Saint brought into the harbor at the same
moment. Inez wanted everyone to stop making her wedding a racing
exhibition. Cassius looked at her. You met me at a race. I also met
you standing still occasionally. We can build on that. She turned to
me. You'll come? Nigga, try to stop me. She hugged me hard.

18
00:06:09,128 --> 00:06:31,369
Cassius waited until she stepped away, then took my hand and pulled me
into his own embrace. My father, he said quietly. I know. My life.
Nigga, you helped save mine too. He stepped back, eyes bright. You
ever need us. I know. This time the words meant exactly what they
should. Celadon kept command of the Sovereign Sun.

19
00:06:31,619 --> 00:06:52,004
I told him the flagship came with the fleet, but the wheel stayed with
the man who knew its name. Renee moved her things aboard the same
afternoon and began rearranging his cabin with a confidence that made
him look happier than any crown could have. He showed me the bridge
before we left. The brass fittings shone.

20
00:06:52,254 --> 00:07:15,204
The little white bird had been restored above the doorway. His old
logbook lay open on the desk, the first new entry written in a steady
hand. HOME. One word. Nigga had earned the period. Marcellus came with
us to the harbor farewell wearing the Blue Mercy ring and a clean
linen suit. He handed Shawna a small silver box.

21
00:07:15,454 --> 00:07:39,154
Inside were earrings shaped like two little waves. For the room, he
said. She looked at him. Earrings? You are most of what makes it
beautiful. Nigga, the old man still had dangerous hands even when he
wasn't holding tools. Shawna kissed his cheek. I shook my head. You
trying to take my job? I retired from competing with young men. They
make it exhausting.

22
00:07:39,404 --> 00:08:02,720
We laughed together. Knox, Tank and Rosa flew back to Vegas a day
ahead of us. Knox said the department needed her. Tank said the
original black Mercedes had been waiting long enough and he wanted to
make sure Rosa's seat was exactly how she'd left it. Rosa said both
niggas were planning something and she intended to be present when it
became obvious.

23
00:08:02,970 --> 00:08:27,024
They took Mercedes and Porsche with them to handle the mainland
arrangements. The new clubs would run through Alina and the island
team. The women could own something without standing beside it every
minute to prove it belonged to them. My police Lamborghini went home
on the earlier cargo flight too, cleaned and repaired again, its gold
badge catching the light as it was loaded.

24
00:08:27,274 --> 00:08:49,157
The same car that had crossed yachts, market stairs, a floating road
and the duke's palace gates would be waiting when I landed in Vegas.
Nigga, some vehicles deserve a vacation. Mine was getting a change of
scenery. On our last afternoon, a black launch entered the harbor
without music. That was the first thing I noticed.

25
00:08:49,407 --> 00:09:14,426
Everything else arriving that week had announced itself with horns,
cheers, somebody waving a bottle. This boat moved quietly to the
private quay. A man in a dark uniform stepped off it and walked toward
the palace. The stranger. The nigga who had watched the duke lose. He
came onto the terrace while Shawna and I were drinking coffee with
Celadon, Renee, Nero and Esteban.

26
00:09:14,676 --> 00:09:36,928
He stopped at a respectful distance and inclined his head. Captain
Aiden. I set down my cup. You keep showing up. I wanted to see whether
the island suited you. Nigga, it adjusted. A faint smile. General
Solomon Saint. The name meant something to Celadon. I saw his
shoulders tighten. Nero looked up from his glass.

27
00:09:37,178 --> 00:10:01,261
Saint was fifty-one, composed, broad through the chest, dark uniform
plain except for a small emblem at the throat: a crown with seven
points. He carried no visible weapon. He had the stillness of a man
accustomed to other people carrying enough for him. You were Aurelio's
friend? I asked. An interested guest. Your interest look expensive. It
can be.

28
00:10:01,511 --> 00:10:25,282
He looked toward the harbor, the fleet, the road climbing past the
opera house. I offered him a festival. Ships. Champions.
Demonstrations of power. He wanted to remain the largest thing in
every room. Nigga, poor timing. Saint smiled more openly. Indeed.
Shawna put her cup down. What do you want from my husband? He turned
toward her with a formal bow.

29
00:10:25,532 --> 00:10:46,341
To find out whether the stories are large enough. They've been trying
to catch up, she said. I loved her so much I almost forgot to dislike
him. Saint took a black envelope from his jacket and laid it on the
table. The seven-point crown shone on its seal. A challenge, he said.
When you return to Las Vegas.

30
00:10:46,591 --> 00:11:10,688
I believe a man who wins every road on one island should have the
opportunity to meet the rest of the world. I didn't touch the envelope
yet. Nigga, you selling tickets or trouble? Sometimes the distinction
is unprofitable. Celadon spoke before I could answer. The island isn't
a weapons fair. Saint looked at him. No, he said. Not under its
present captain.

31
00:11:10,938 --> 00:11:31,941
He let the sentence sit there, pleasant enough to be heard two ways
and ugly in both. I stood. He looked back at me. My island. My people.
My wife. If you got a challenge, put your own name on the risk. For
the first time something bright moved behind his still eyes. I intend
to. He stepped away from the table.

32
00:11:32,191 --> 00:11:54,985
Enjoy your return, Captain. Then he left as quietly as he had arrived.
I watched the black launch cross the harbor. Nero put down his glass.
That man doesn't collect trophies. He collects the men holding them.
Nigga, he picked a heavy shelf. Shawna took the envelope and turned it
over in her hands. You don't have to answer today. I know.

33
00:11:55,235 --> 00:12:16,406
You have a home to get back to. I looked at her. Then at the island.
Two homes now, at least. More if you counted every place my people had
made room at a table and expected me to show up hungry. We go home, I
said. She smiled. I called Tank that evening. "Nigga, the Mercedes
good?" "The Mercedes good.

34
00:12:16,656 --> 00:12:39,079
The nigga driving it good. His woman good. Why you checking on the car
first?" "Because you answered. I already knew you alive." Rosa took
the phone. "Nigga, he washed it twice." "That's care." "Then he sat in
it waiting for you." Tank's voice came from farther away. "Nigga, I
was checking the seat." "This nigga loves you," Rosa told me.

35
00:12:39,329 --> 00:12:58,152
I smiled at the dark sea beyond the terrace. "Tell that nigga I know.
Tell him I'm coming." The next morning the harbor came to say goodbye.
Not every person. Enough to make the road look like it had grown an
audience. Celadon rang the bell. Renee waved from the bridge.

36
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:22,723
Lark and Mateo stood beneath the garage sign, both holding coffee,
both finally looking like people allowed to plan a week. Mercedes and
Porsche called from Vegas while Alina held the phone toward the crowd
so they could shout their own goodbyes into it. Cassius and Inez drove
us to the airfield in the White Heron, Nero following in a second car
with Esteban.

37
00:13:22,973 --> 00:13:45,464
On the way, Inez took one bend too quickly just to hear Cassius
complain. Nigga, this is my father's car. Your father taught you to be
brave. He also taught me to stop talking to you while driving. She
laughed and reached for his hand at the next straight. At the plane, I
hugged them both. Take care of my ocean, I told Inez.

38
00:13:45,714 --> 00:14:08,791
Take care of the road between here and us. Always. We boarded with the
island deed in my case, seven keys wrapped carefully beside it,
Shawna's music in the blue bag and the black envelope waiting unopened
in the inner pocket of my jacket. Marcellus sat across the aisle,
already asleep before the plane moved. Shawna took the window seat.

39
00:14:09,042 --> 00:14:31,177
I took the one beside her. As we climbed, Isla Gloria shrank beneath
us. The palace became white stone. The harbor became a curve of light.
The roads became little lines I knew with my hands. My wife rested her
head on my shoulder. You really got me the ocean. Nigga, I pay
attention. She laughed softly.

40
00:14:31,427 --> 00:14:52,618
Then she fell asleep with her hand over mine. Hours later, the lights
of Vegas appeared beneath the wing. I looked down at the city where
the whole beautiful disaster had begun. Somewhere below, my black
Mercedes was waiting with Tank beside it. My police Lamborghini was
clean for perhaps the last time that week.

41
00:14:52,868 --> 00:15:16,591
My chief had a department full of niggas who had watched me win an
island and apparently still believed I needed supervision. Shawna woke
as the wheels touched down. Home? she asked. I kissed her. Home. The
black envelope pressed against my chest beside Dante's cross. General
Saint could wait until I saw what Vegas had done with my name.

42
00:15:16,841 --> 00:15:21,064
Nigga, I had been gone a month. The city had better have used it.
